  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 119 PM CDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nThe hot and mainly dry weather pattern persists heading into Friday \nlasting through the forecast period. This is thanks to the upper \nridge of high pressure positioned across the Great Basin to just \nwest of the Four Corners region. Easterly to northeasterly flow \naloft on the fringe of the high pressure will keep temperatures in \nthe low to upper 90s. Areas along the Pecos River and Rio Grande \nwill top out in the low 100s. Daily low (10-30%) chances of isolated \nshowers/storms are in store across the higher terrain and far West \nTexas due to upslope flow and shortwave impulses rounding the \nperiphery of the ridge. Most locations are going to remain dry. Low \ntemperatures are expected to range from the 60s to mid 70s \nregionwide each night. \n\nLamberson",
